{"at": "2026-11-19T21:14:37.759Z", "run": "20261119-0033-verify-storage-5b1c", "unit": "u02", "op": "set", "rid": "storage/openicpsr-self-publishing-repository", "path": "$.reliability_note", "old": "Long-running (ICPSR since 1962) with DOI permanence and version history; the failure mode is editorial/scope rejection, not data loss or throttling.", "new": "The former openICPSR self-publishing platform has been fully integrated into ICPSR; deposits go through the Thematic Data Collections and the Where to Deposit Your Data page. Self-published data are now screened for inappropriate content, are viewable in the ICPSR catalog within 40 business hours rather than published immediately, and are no longer assigned a DOI or published on acceptance. Scope/editorial rejection remains the failure mode.", "rung": "documented", "evidence": {"url": "https://www.openicpsr.org/openicpsr/faqs", "date": "2026-11-19", "proved": "self-published data are now screened, delayed up to 40 business hours, and get no DOI", "capture": "sha256:eb78f24206e90b0a79f641efc245af1518ecba7791e160c2896acca2f32c512e", "quote": "NEW: Self-published data will no longer be assigned a persistent identifier (DOI) or be published immediately, but they will be viewable in ICPSR’s catalog within 40 business hours."}, "added": true, "reason": "The current first-party FAQ documents that the service was integrated into ICPSR and that self-published deposits are now screened, delayed and no longer get a DOI."}
